---
import extensions from "../../captures/extensions.png";
import Callout from "../../guide/Callout.astro";
import GuidePage from "../../guide/GuidePage.astro";
import Path from "../../guide/Path.astro";
import Task from "../../guide/Task.astro";
import { sitePath } from "../../site/links.ts";
---

<GuidePage manual="docs" slug="extension-stores" lead="Titles come from sources, sources come in extensions, and extension stores list the extensions you can install.">
  <Task id="add" title="Add a store">
    <ol>
      <li>
        Open <Path>Browse › Extensions</Path>, then <Path>⋮ › Extension stores</Path>. With no store yet, the empty list has an
        <strong>Extension stores</strong> button too.
      </li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Add</strong>, paste the store's address into <strong>Store index URL</strong>, and tap <strong>Add</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Stores made for Mihon, Aniyomi or LNReader are added the same way.
      <a href={sitePath("docs/extension-compatibility/")}>Extension compatibility</a> lists which of their extensions Katari loads, and
      what changes for <a href={sitePath("docs/extension-compatibility/#not-signed")}>stores that don't sign their extensions</a>.
    </p>
    <Callout label="Choose stores you trust">
      <p>Katari has no affiliation with any store or source. A malicious extension can read stored logins and run any code it likes, so add only stores you trust.</p>
    </Callout>
  </Task>

  <Task id="install" title="Install and update extensions" shot={{ image: extensions, alt: "An installed extension that supplies comics, video and books", caption: "Extensions" }}>
    <ol>
      <li>On <Path>Browse › Extensions</Path>, tap the download button beside an extension to install it.</li>
      <li>When a store has a newer version, the extension moves under <strong>Updates pending</strong>. Tap <strong>Update</strong> beside it, or <strong>Update all</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      One extension can supply comics, video and books. To see only the kinds you want, tap the filter button and pick them under
      <strong>Content types</strong>.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="trust" title="Trust an extension">
    <p>
      Katari runs an extension straight away when it is signed with the key of a store you added. One installed some other way shows as
      <strong>Untrusted</strong> until you tap the shield beside it and confirm with <strong>Trust</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      That trust covers one version only, so each update of such an extension asks again. <Path>Settings › Advanced › Revoke trusted unknown
      extensions</Path> takes it back from all of them.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="remove" title="Remove a store">
    <p>
      In <Path>Browse › Extensions › ⋮ › Extension stores</Path>, tap the delete button beside the store and confirm. Extensions you
      installed from it keep working, but they show as <strong>Orphaned</strong> and get no more updates.
    </p>
  </Task>
</GuidePage>
